{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795558084,"nonce":"P1oEbRJU7LhBVU5b52SqiFcel28=","title":"Rich text editor in blinc_cn: cn toolbar, icons, toolbar modes, alignment, lists, tables","message":"The owner's requests on 2026-11-24, in order given:\n\n1. Move the rich text editor from blinc_layout to blinc_cn, so its toolbar can use cn components and its colour button the existing cn colour picker.\n2. Update the website's component demo and the Blinc book with it.\n3. Proper icons in the toolbar. Reference: a rounded floating bar of icon buttons (bold, italic, underline, strikethrough, link), a vertical divider and a close button, a tooltip naming the hovered button, and a pointer toward the selection.\n4. Alignment options, inline table or grid placement, and lists, in the toolbar and the editor.\n5. Switch between the floating selection toolbar and a fixed toolbar above the text. Reference: a card whose top row holds bold, italic, underline, link, align left/centre/right, a list menu (checklist icon with a chevron), a colour dot, link, code and image buttons.\n\nDone so far: the move (1), with the book page under the cn section, a 0.6 to 0.7 migration page and the catalog entry pointed at the new module.\n\nWhat the editor already has to build on: Block kinds and their rendering (render.rs, document.rs), marks (format.rs), the selection toolbar (toolbar.rs) with an inline preset palette, a heading row and a link draft that the editor captures keystrokes into, so focus never leaves the editor.\n\nDesign points to settle while building:\n- The cn colour picker and cn input take focus; the editor must keep its selection and toolbar while they have it, or the pickers stay inline in the toolbar.\n- Alignment is a block property (left, centre, right, justify) that wrapping and rendering must follow, and Markdown export has no syntax for it.\n- Lists: check which list kinds BlockKind already has (bullet, numbered, task) and add the missing ones with indent levels.\n- Tables or grids inline in a document are a new block kind with cell editing, navigation and Markdown table export.","files":null}]}